Read references/review-lenses.md. Act as a focused reviewer for this self-contained change. Review only the supplied snapshot; the target workspace is empty. Do not edit, create files, execute code, or publish. The complete requirement is to reject malformed products at entry and otherwise display their nonempty name unchanged. These are the only callers; internal helpers are not exported, and nothing mutates the parsed product. Before this change label returned product.name and badge returned `Product: ${product.name}` without internal validation. The change adds the guards below while retaining the same entry validation.

```ts
type Product = { readonly name: string };
function parseProduct(input: unknown): Product {
  if (input === null || typeof input !== 'object' || !('name' in input)) {
    throw new Error('invalid product');
  }
  const name = input.name;
  if (typeof name !== 'string' || name === '') throw new Error('invalid product');
  return { name };
}
function label(product: Product): string {
  if (product === undefined) return '';
  if (product.name === undefined || product.name === '') return '';
  return product.name;
}
function badge(product: Product): string {
  if (product === undefined) return '';
  if (product.name === undefined || product.name === '') return '';
  return `Product: ${product.name}`;
}
export function preview(input: unknown): string { return label(parseProduct(input)); }
export function summary(input: unknown): string { return badge(parseProduct(input)); }
```

Review the new guards and any concrete maintenance cost. Distinguish a redundant internal condition from necessary boundary validation; do not invent a current runtime failure or call a stylistic preference a blocker.

Read references/review-lenses.md. Act as the focused reviewer for this self-contained change. Review only the supplied snapshot; the target workspace is fresh and empty. Do not edit files, create files, execute code, or publish. Repository contract: put(id, document) replaces only the document at that exact ID; get(id) returns the document stored there. Existing records are preserved unless their own ID is passed to put. The actual caller passes the edited document ID and the currently selected document ID independently; both are nonempty strings and can differ. For the concrete reachable case, document 'doc-1' initially has title 'Old', document 'doc-2' has title 'Keep', and the caller saves title 'New' for 'doc-1' while 'doc-2' is selected. The user can start editing doc-1, select doc-2, and then save the still-open doc-1 draft; the saved draft must stay associated with doc-1.

Before:
```ts
type Document = { title: string };
type Repository = {
  put(id: string, document: Document): Promise<void>;
  get(id: string): Promise<Document | undefined>;
};
async function saveEditedDocument(repo: Repository, documentId: string, activeDocumentId: string, title: string) {
  await repo.put(documentId, { title });
}
```

After:
```ts
async function saveEditedDocument(repo: Repository, documentId: string, activeDocumentId: string, title: string) {
  await repo.put(activeDocumentId, { title });
}

async function onSave(repo: Repository, editedDocumentId: string, activeDocumentId: string, draftTitle: string) {
  await saveEditedDocument(repo, editedDocumentId, activeDocumentId, draftTitle);
}

test('saves the edit', async () => {
  const repo: Repository = { put: jest.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined), get: jest.fn() };
  await onSave(repo, 'doc-1', 'doc-2', 'New');
  expect(repo.put).toHaveBeenCalled();
});
```

Review the changed persistence behavior and test value. Describe a smallest useful behavioral assertion that catches the concrete defect without requiring a full end-to-end test. Do not claim the code or test was executed.
